# Adding code with gortisan

This project was created by gortisan, which writes code into it but is not a
dependency. Run it through the script in the project root — it runs the
gortisan version the project pins:

- `./gortisan` on macOS, Linux and Git Bash; `gortisan.bat` or `.\gortisan.ps1` on Windows.

| To add | Run |
|---|---|
| A feature (entity, service, storage, handler, DTO, routes, test) | `./gortisan make:feature <name> [--fields "a:string,b:int"] [--soft-delete]` |
| An endpoint of a feature | `./gortisan make:handler <feature>/<action>` (list, get, create, update, delete, or any name) |
{{- if .Migrations}}
| A schema change | `./gortisan make:migration <name>`, then `go run . migrate up` |
{{- end}}
| An enum | `./gortisan make:enum <feature>/<name> --members "a,b,c"` |
| A reusable validator | `./gortisan make:validator <group>/<name>` |
| A client for one of our services / a third-party API | `./gortisan make:client <name>` / `./gortisan make:external <name>` |
| A middleware | `./gortisan make:middleware <name>` |
| A test | `./gortisan make:test <feature>` or `./gortisan make:test <feature>/<action>` |

Then:

1. Read what the command printed: it lists anything left to do by hand.
2. Fill in the generated code (the handler body, the DTO fields, the SQL).
{{- if .Swagger}}
3. Run `./gortisan swag` when a handler's swag comments changed.
{{- end}}
4. Run `go test ./...` — it includes `tests/arch_test.go`, which fails when a
   feature imports another feature or shared code imports a feature.

`./gortisan route:list` shows every endpoint; `./gortisan list` every command.
